---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { liveTools } from '../data/tools';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const tools = liveTools();
---

<Page
	title="About Handy – Free, Private Online Tools"
	description="Handy offers free tools for PDFs, photos, invoices and CVs that run in your browser, so your files never leave your device."
	heading="About Handy"
>
	<p>
		Handy is a collection of free online tools for everyday jobs: merging a PDF for a job portal, shrinking a photo so it
		uploads on a slow connection, making an invoice for a customer, or getting a passport photo ready for an application.
	</p>

	<h2>Why we built it</h2>
	<p>
		Many free tools online ask you to upload your files to a server you know nothing about. That is a real worry when the
		file is a certificate, an ID card or a bank detail. They can also be slow and heavy on mobile data.
	</p>
	<p>
		Handy works differently. Our tools run <strong>inside your own browser</strong>, on your own phone or computer. Your
		documents and photos are not uploaded to us, so we never see them. It is also light on data, because the pages are
		small and each tool loads only what it needs.
	</p>

	<h2>What you can do here</h2>
	<ul>
		{tools.map((t) => <li><a href={`/${t.slug}`}>{t.name}</a>: {t.summary}</li>)}
	</ul>
	<p>We are adding more tools over time, including calculators and helpers for everyday work.</p>

	<h2>Our promises</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Private by design.</strong> Your files stay on your device. Read the details on our <a href="/privacy">Privacy page</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>Free to use.</strong> No account, no sign-up. The site may show ads in future to cover its costs.</li>
		<li><strong>Honest about limits.</strong> If a tool cannot do something well, we say so on the page instead of pretending.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Who runs Handy</h2>
	<p>
		Handy is built and run by an independent developer in {site.country}. If something is broken, confusing or missing,
		please tell us on the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. We read every message.
	</p>
</Page>
